   "subject": "Existing Rmd file to Notebook?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "HI!\r<br>Is it possible to make an existing Rmd file to work as Notebook?\r<br>(i.e. by including some special configuration commands)\r<br>\r<br>Thanks\r<br>Agus\r<br>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "wxNj18pIEQAJ",
   "from": "Jeff Newmiller",
   "author": "8502567f9dbc7c7e",
   "date": "2016-12-16T14:46:51Z",
   "subject": "Re: [knitr] Existing Rmd file to Notebook?",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"auto\">You are thinking of the RStudio v1.0 display feature, not a feature of knitr. AFAIK any rmarkdown file (with the YAML header) will be displayed as if it were a notebook in RStudio v1.0, but a definitive answer would have to come from RStudio support.</div><div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\">On Dec 16, 2016 1:52 AM, &quot;Agustin Lobo&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">alobo...@gmail.com</a>&gt; wrote:<br type=\"attribution\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote style=\"margin:0 0 0 .8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\">HI!<br>\r\nIs it possible to make an existing Rmd file to work as Notebook?<br>\r\n(i.e. by including some special configuration commands)<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThanks<br>\r\nAgus<br>\r\n</blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
